TI  - Non-invasive pulse signal acquisition system for            facilitating pulse detection and prediction of heart            diseases, has standard database comprising sensors,            data acquisition equipment, filter, amplifier and            analog-to-digital converter
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a standard database comprising                sensors, a data acquisition (DAQ) equipment, a DAQ                device, a filter, an amplifier and an                analog-to-digital (A/D) converter (11). A                force-sensing resistor (FSR) detects changes in                force applied caused by a pulse. The DAQ device                measures voltage change and imports data to LabVIEW                (RTM: system-design platform and development                environment for a visual programming language) for                analysis. A DAQ assistant obtains voltage change                with respect to ground. A Butter worth filter                attenuates ambient noise.
                    USE - Non-invasive pulse signal acquisition system                for facilitating pulse detection and prediction of                heart diseases i.e. cardiac arrhythmia such as                bradychardia and tachycardia, by detecting three                pulse pressure points e.g. kough, vatta and pitta,                of a person based on virtual instrument technology                using LabVIEW (RTM: system-design platform and                development environment for a visual programming                language) software.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system realizes pulse detection and                prediction of heart diseases with maximum accuracy                using cost effective non-invasive process. The                system can accurately describe condition of a                subject and measure heart rates ranging from 50 -                220 bpm. The system utilizes compact and feasible                technique for detection of radial pulse and                differentiation between three pressure                points.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a signal                processing unit in LABVIEW.Preamplifier (7)High pass filter (8)Low pass filter (9)Post amplifier (10)A/D converter (11)
