TY  - JOUR
AU  - Du, Haixia
AU  - Li, Zhenzhen
TI  - ANALYSIS OF THE IMPACT OF THE ECOLOGICAL ENVIRONMENT ON THE RAILWAY CONSTRUCTION BASED ON ANALYTIC HIERARCHY PROCESS (AHP) AND PROBABILITY STATISTICS
T2  - FRESENIUS ENVIRONMENTAL BULLETIN
M3  - Article
AB  - Eco-environmental impact assessment is a process of comprehensively analysing the characteristics of the ecological environment and development and construction activities and their interaction. This article summarizes the current situation of the ecological environmental impact assessment of railway construction projects, points out its unreasonable points, and proposes new methods for assessment. At the same time, it studies the formulation principles of the comprehensive evaluation index system of railway ecological environmental impact, establishes reasonable evaluation indicators, and aims to explore a method that can quantify the ecological impact evaluation which is highly operable and comparable. We use the improved analytic hierarchy process (AHP) to determine the weights, reducing the error that may be caused by artificially determining the weights. The experiment designed a sample combination consisting of n samples, and there is a measured index matrix X (mxn), and passed c Level standard evaluation suppresses m indicators. Using the constructed probability and statistics method, the pattern recognition model and the probability and statistics method, we input of the integrated unit system as 1 (t x c) fuzzy matrix, and determine the corresponding grade standard. Theevaluation value is 0.53, and the evaluation grade is 3. Judging from the current research situation of some scholars, there are more qualitative evaluations on ecological impacts, but less quantitative evaluations. Considering that an index system should be established based on the characteristics of railway construction itself, and railway projects should be divided into subgrade engineering, bridge engineering, tunnel engineering, etc., each project should be refined into each process, and the characteristics of each process should be analyzed to extract factors affecting the environment. We establish an indicator system, which includes (1) water pollution control, (2) noise pollution control, (3) air pollution control, (4) solid waste control, (5) damage to the ecological environment, (6) the health of construction workers affects. Based on the research data of ecological environmental impact assessment of construction projects at home and abroad, this paper analyzes the relationship between railway construction and the ecological environment in detail in accordance with the characteristics of the railway ecological environmental impact, and finds out the possible negative impacts on the ecological environment. The jury is composed of 10 experts. According to the specific situation and relevant information, combined with various indicators, the judgement set P = [A, B, C, D, E] is judged, indicating that the magnitude of the impact is on the environment. The review weighting coefficient matrix is F. At the same time, the comprehensive evaluation evaluates the railway ecological project, making the ecological environment impact assessment project more scientific and reasonable. The results show that this method is also suitable for solving other similar problems.
