AU  - HOOPER M J
TI  - Marine electronics system for monitoring noise            level of fishing vessel, has marine electronics device            which is configured to generate noise level indicator            for display on user interface, based on passive sonar            data
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (405) has a transducer element                configured to receive active sonar returns from                sonar signals emitted into an underwater                environment during first time period. The active                sonar returns are used to generate one or more                sonar images. The passive sonar data corresponding                to ambient noise associated with the vessel is                received during second time period different from                the first time period. A marine electronics device                has a processor (410) configured to receive the                passive sonar data from the transducer assembly,                and generate a noise level indicator indicating an                ambient noise level associated with the vessel                based on the passive sonar data. The noise level                indicator is displayed on an user interface (435)                of the marine electronics device.
                    USE - Marine electronics system for monitoring noise                level of fishing vessel.
                    ADVANTAGE - The noise level indicator alerts personnel on                the watercraft of a high noise condition associated                with the vessel, and thus, prompting action to                reduce or eliminate the noise during fishing                operations. The noise level indicator also                identifies abnormal noise levels indicative of                equipment malfunction or failure, and/or improper                watercraft operation such as improper trim or                ballast, in addition to identifying noise to                improve fishing.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                of indicating an ambient noise level associated                with a vessel.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of marine                electronics system.Marine electronics system (405)Processor (410)Memory (420)User interface (435)Display (440)
