TI  - Portable oxygen concentrator system for use in            vehicle, has compressor to draw and compress ambient            air, filtration system operatively connected to            compressor, product tank operatively connected to            filtration system, delivery mechanism to deliver            oxygen-enriched air from product tank to patient
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The portable oxygen concentrator system for                use in a vehicle, has: a compressor to draw ambient                air and compress the ambient air to higher                pressure; a filtration system operatively connected                to the compressor, where the filtration system                comprises a first sieve bed and a second sieve bed,                first sieve bed and second sieve bed contains                zeolite material to absorb nitrogen molecules from                the ambient air; a product tank operatively                connected to the filtration system, where the                product tank stores oxygen-enriched air; a delivery                mechanism to deliver the oxygen-enriched air from                the product tank to a patient via a nasal cannula;                a cooling system to dissipate excess heat generated                during compression and filtration processes; an                oxygen level indicator to monitor oxygen                concentration within the vehicle and alert                passengers when the oxygen concentration falls                below a predetermined threshold.
                    USE - Portable oxygen concentrator system for use in                a vehicle.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system ensures continuous supply of                oxygen-enriched air to a patient while monitoring                and adjusting the oxygen levels based on real-time                readings. The oxygen concentrator system enables                improved air quality within the vehicle, thus                ensuring the patient receives a reliable supply of                oxygen-enriched air. The system's automatic                adjustment mechanism ensures that oxygen delivery                is responsive to the patient's needs, enhancing                patient safety and comfort. The cooling system                enhances heat dissipation from the compressor and                filtration system such a configuration enables the                prevention of overheating, thus enhancing the                system's operational efficiency and longevity. The                oxygen level indicator comprises a voice alert                mechanism configured to notify passengers of low                oxygen concentration levels through audible alerts.                Moreover, such a mechanism ensures timely awareness                of oxygen levels, enhancing passenger safety. The                automatic adjustment mechanism is configured to                interface with the oximeter through a wireless                communication protocol to receive the real-time                readings. Moreover, such an interface enables                accurate and timely adjustments to oxygen delivery,                enhancing patient care. The noise reduction system                minimizes operational noise within the vehicle.                Moreover, such a reduction system enhances                passenger comfort by reducing noise pollution                inside the vehicle. The system ensures                uninterrupted oxygen supply, thus enhancing system                reliability. The entire system, from air intake to                oxygen delivery, is designed to provide a reliable,                portable solution for oxygen therapy, ensuring                patients' health and mobility are maintained                effectively.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - The portable oxygen concentrator system for                use in a vehicle, has: a compressor to draw ambient                air and compress the ambient air to higher                pressure; a filtration system operatively connected                to the compressor, where the filtration system                comprises a first sieve bed and a second sieve bed,                first sieve bed and second sieve bed contains                zeolite material to absorb nitrogen molecules from                the ambient air; a product tank operatively                connected to the filtration system, where the                product tank stores oxygen-enriched air; a delivery                mechanism to deliver the oxygen-enriched air from                the product tank to a patient via a nasal cannula;                a cooling system to dissipate excess heat generated                during compression and filtration processes; an                oxygen level indicator to monitor oxygen                concentration within the vehicle and alert                passengers when the oxygen concentration falls                below a predetermined threshold; an automatic                adjustment mechanism to modify the output of the                oxygen-enriched air based on real-time readings                from an oximeter; a dedicated air intake passage                configured to allow fresh air from outside the                vehicle to reach the compressor; and a placement                configuration under a backseat of the vehicle,                providing accessibility and protection from direct                sunlight and potential damage.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a portable oxygen                concentrator system for use in a vehicle.
