AU  - Miyake, Tsugunobu
AU  - Marchiori, Alan
A1  - IEEE
TI  - A Continuous Turbidity Meter with Synchronous Detection
T2  - 2024 IEEE APPLIED SENSING CONFERENCE, APSCON
M3  - Proceedings Paper
CP  - 25th IEEE Applied Sensing Conference (IEEE APSCON)
CL  - INDIA
AB  - Access to clean water is a United Nations Sustainable Development Goal [1]. Turbidity is one fundamental indicator of water quality. A continuous turbidity meter can be integrated into drinking water systems to assess source and treated water quality. Previous work has developed handheld sample-based meters, but little work is available for a continuous, flow-through, turbidity meter. This paper develops a continuous turbidity meter using synchronous detection to reduce ambient noise in the measurement. The meter was tested and performed similarly to previous sample-based meters; in the range 0 to 60 FNU we found a standard error of 0.31 FNU; additional tests below 16 FNU yielded a standard error of 0.105 FNU. A sensitivity analysis verified that two-point calibration was sufficient to calibrate the meter. These results suggest the developed meter could be useful to monitor and improve clean water access in under and limited resourced regions.
