TI  - Method for adjusting message indicators of            wireless telephone based on environmental conditions,            involves adjusting characteristic of one of message            indicators based on condition of environmental in which            communication device is located
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves detecting a condition of                environment in which a mobile communication device                is located, using an environmental sampling sensor                (148), where the condition includes ambient audio                and ambient light. Characteristic of one of message                indicators is adjusted based on the detected                condition if the detected condition satisfies a                prescribed criterion when a state of the device is                changed upon receipt of an incoming message, where                the characteristics include a ringer volume level,                a display brightness or color scheme, and a                vibration intensity of a haptic feedback                mechanism.
                    USE - Method for adjusting message indicators of a                mobile communication device i.e. wireless telephone                with function of personal digital assistant and/or                music player, based on environmental conditions                e.g. ambient audio and ambient light (all claimed).                Can also be used for a laptop computer, tablet                computer, smartphone and netbook.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables providing notification to a                user of an incoming call, text, email or other                message by automatically increasing or decreasing                the audio, haptic, visual or other message                indicator levels generated by the mobile                communications device to compensate for noisy                environments, depending on the environment in which                the mobile communications device is located. The                method enables adjusting the message indicators                based on the ambient audio level in loud                environment such that the speaker volume can be                automatically increased, the mobile communications                device is made to vibrate more strongly and/or with                increased frequency, or brightness of the mobile                communications device display is increased to                notify the incoming call, text or email in                environments with high ambient noise when the user                is listening to music.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included for the                following:(1) a mobile communication device(2) computer-readable storage media comprising                a set of instructions for adjusting message                indicators employed by a mobile communication                device to notify a user regarding change in state                or status of the device based on environmental                conditions.
