AU  - PATRICELLI, G.
TI  - THE IMPACT OF ANTHROPOGENIC NOISE ON BIRD POPULATION AND BEHAVIOR
M3  - Awarded Grant
AB  - There has been a growing recognition in recent years that noise pollution may have profound and widespread impacts on wildlife, yet we know remarkably little about the extent and magnitude of these impacts. One way that noise may affect animals is by disrupting communication, which plays a central role in animal social and reproductive life. My team will address the impacts of noise pollution on birds in two main projects: first, measuring the impacts of noise from energy development on greater sage-grouse (Centrocercus urophasianus), and second, measuring how local songbirds adjust their vocalizations in response to noise from roads and urban development.
