TI  - Method for operating manufacturing or analyzing            device for semiconductor wafers, involves detecting            event during operation of device based on processed            electrical signal and controlling operation of device            according to detected event
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves detecting sound in a                process chamber (100) of the device during                operation of a manufacturing or analysis device                (10). An electrical signal corresponding to the                detected sound is obtained through a signal                processor (310). The received electrical signal is                processed by the signal processor. An event during                operation of the device is detected based on the                processed electrical signal. The operation of the                device is controlled according to the detected                event.
                    USE - Method for operating manufacturing or                analyzing device for semiconductor wafers of system                for manufacturing or analyzing semiconductor wafers                (all claimed), used for monitoring operating                conditions of devices to detect abnormal behavior                such as mechanical fault, mechanical failure,                collision of several portions, wafer scratch by                movable or stationary portion of equipment,                collision of moving portion, loosening of portions,                accumulation of particles or dusts, mistreatment of                wafer, misalignment of wafer to handler and                abnormal gas flow when gas is injected into chamber                or gas is sucked or evacuated from chamber. Uses                include but are not limited to electroluminescent                display, atomic layer deposition (ALD) apparatus,                epitaxial growth apparatus, ion implantation                device, wet processing device, critical dimension                measuring device (CD), scanning electron microscope                (SEM), heterodyne measuring device, defect                inspection device and measuring device for                electrical properties.
                    ADVANTAGE - The signal processor filters the electrical                signals received by each of the microphones, such                that the ambient noise is reduced and the                signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) is improved. The moving                portions wear out due to wear by long-term                operation which causes change in the characteristic                noise or vibration. The central server and the                device controller predict or estimate the next                maintenance time so that mechanical failure that                damages the wafer and the device is prevented. The                abnormal operation of the semiconductor                manufacturing or analyzing device is effectively                detected by detecting and analyzing characteristic                noises generated by the moving portions of                semiconductor manufacturing or analyzing device.                The next maintenance time is predicted and thus                damage to the wafer and the device is prevented by                monitoring the characteristic noises.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a device                for manufacturing or analyzing semiconductor                wafers.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic view of the                device for semiconductor manufacturing operation in                normal operation.Manufacturing or analysis device (10)Process chamber (100)Microphone (250)Signal processor (310)Device controller (320)
